<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof Completions of Initial Observations</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proposition 3.5 Proof Completion</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To show more explicitly that <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> has a policy with zero error, consider the policy <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:\{1,2\}\times\{0,1,2,\delta\}^{2}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:\{1,2\}\times\{0,1,2,\delta\}^{2}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> defined by:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M(i,a_{1},a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M(i,a_{1},a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}1&amp;a_{1},a_{2}\in\{0,1,2\},a_{i}=(a_{-i}+1)\mod 3\\
0&amp;a_{1},a_{2}\in\{0,1,2\},a_{i}=(a_{-i}-1)\mod 3\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;a_{1},a_{2}\in\{0,1,2\},a_{1}=a_{2}\\
1&amp;a_{i}\in\{0,1,2\},a_{-i}=\delta\\
0&amp;a_{i}=\delta,a_{-i}\in\{0,1,2\}\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;a_{1}=a_{2}=\delta\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}1&amp;a_{1},a_{2}\in\{0,1,2\},a_{i}=(a_{-i}+1)\mod 3\\
0&amp;a_{1},a_{2}\in\{0,1,2\},a_{i}=(a_{-i}-1)\mod 3\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;a_{1},a_{2}\in\{0,1,2\},a_{1}=a_{2}\\
1&amp;a_{i}\in\{0,1,2\},a_{-i}=\delta\\
0&amp;a_{i}=\delta,a_{-i}\in\{0,1,2\}\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;a_{1}=a_{2}=\delta\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Lastly, let’s note that not only can we say that every policy for <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has strictly positive error, we furthermore know that every policy for <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has error at least <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{6}</annotation></semantics></math>. We get this lower bound from Theorem 5.5: <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly the PIDDG constructed in the proof of Theorem 5.5 when <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=3,n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=3,n=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proposition 3.6 Proof Completion</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To show that our CKDDG has a policy whose error is strictly less than the minimum error among policies which map to <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the policy <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:\{1,2\}\times\{0,1,2,3,\delta\}^{2}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:\{1,2\}\times\{0,1,2,3,\delta\}^{2}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(1,\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(1,\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ A.2 Proposition 3.6 Proof Completion ‣ Appendix A Proof Completions of Initial Observations ‣ Designing Rules for Choosing a Winner in a Debate" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> has zero error in anonymous scenarios <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>. In anonymous scenario <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, the value for the desired loser is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (the desired loser can guarantee at least <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by playing action <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> while the desired winner can guarantee at most <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by uniformly playing <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>). In anonymous scenario <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>, the value for the desired loser is also <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (the desired loser can guarantee at least <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by uniformly mixing over <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the desired winner can guarantee at most <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by playing action <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>). Thus the error of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{6}{100}+\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{4}{100}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{6}{100}+\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{4}{100}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
